DISJOINT DIRECTION COUNTING n=5
============================================================
  (5, 1)-(4, 2) s=(4,2) rov=3: same=2, opp=0, net=2, ratio=2/1
  (4, 1)-(5, 2) s=(3,3) rov=3: same=2, opp=0, net=2, ratio=2/1
  (4, 1)-(5, 3) s=(3,2) rov=2: same=1, opp=0, net=1, ratio=1/1
  (3, 1)-(5, 2) s=(2,3) rov=2: same=1, opp=0, net=1, ratio=1/1
  (3, 1)-(4, 2) s=(2,2) rov=2: same=0, opp=0, net=0, ratio=0/1
  (4, 2)-(5, 3) s=(2,2) rov=2: same=0, opp=0, net=0, ratio=0/1

  The ratio same/opp is always > 1 for disjoint pairs.
  For disjoint pairs with opp=0, the coefficient is entirely from same-dir cycles.
  For pairs with opp>0, same-dir ALWAYS exceeds opp-dir.

